  "question_stem": "A large field of area $4 \\text{ km}^2$ is becoming infected with a soil disease. At time $t$ years the area infected is $x \\text{ km}^2$ and the rate of growth of the infected area is given by the differential equation $$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t} = kx(4 - x),$$ where $k$ is a positive constant. It is given that when $t = 0$, $x = 0.4$ and that when $t = 2$, $x = 2$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$\\ln\\frac{x}{4-x}=t\\ln3-\\ln9$ and $k=\\frac14\\ln3$"
  ],
